  "description": "A welfare-style disbursement program with synthetic beneficiaries (clearly-fake identities/phones only). The seeded policy is DELIBERATELY LOOSE — it only checks category/budget eligibility, nothing else — so a mule-merchant pattern (one merchant, many unrelated beneficiaries, rapid redemptions) and a synthetic duplicate-identity enrollment both go completely undetected on the first run. This is the kit's money shot: a team's agent detects the pattern from the labeled transaction stream, calls propose_rule, a human approves via the HITL inbox, and a rerun of the SAME transactions is now blocked. See README 'The rerun-after-tighten loop'.",
